<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - LIN TELEVISION CUT.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - LIN TELEVISION CUT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salomon Brothers said on Wednesday it lowered its rating on the shares of LIN Television to a hold, after Hicks, Muse, Tate &amp; Furst Inc said it agreed to acquire LIN for $1.7 billion in cash and debt.</p>
<p>-- &quot;We are downgrading the shares of LIN to hold from buy to reflect the $47.50 acquisition price for LIN which has been offered by Hicks, Muse Tate &amp; Furst,&quot; analyst Paul Sweeney said in a research note.</p>
<p>-- Sweeney said he doubted other bids would emerge for LIN and recommended investors swap out of the shares.</p>
<p>-- LIN shares lost 1-15/16 to 46-11/16.</p>
<p>((Wall Street desk 212-859-1730))</p>
